 "notes": "Libretto by Luigi Illica and Giuseppe Giacosa (1896). Words follow the Ricordi vocal score's spelling and punctuation, with its dot runs (dormire........, Mimì.............., presto..............), perchè with the grave accent, \"un'aurora\", Mimì's \"come un tramonto\", \"Mio bel signorino posso ben dirlo adesso,\" (no comma after signorino), and \"buio,e\" printed as one run: in bar 96 \"buio,e\" is sung on one note, in bar 106 \"bu-io,e\" on two. Mimì's quotations in «» are her words from Act 1 (\"Mi chiamano Mimì… il perchè non so\") and Rodolfo's (\"Che gelida manina… Se la lasci riscaldar!\"). IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, words sung on one note joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ, intervocalic s voiced. Translation literal, for meaning.",
